<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.1.5: Simplifying Exponents</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01245</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.1.5: Simplifying Exponents</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0eae6d9a-ed82-4755-8b05-db0b5882f0e9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Complete the table using all of the exponent properties you learned in the lesson.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <table class="os-raise-textheavytable">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis>Expression</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Simplified Result</emphasis></entry></row>
          <row>
          <entry>
            \(j^5 \cdot j^3\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
           \(\frac{h^7}{h^3}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
           \((-ab)^0\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \(\frac{1}{s^{-4}}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((\frac{m}{n})^{-4}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
           \((p^5)^2\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((3s^3t^2)^3\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
          \((\frac{b}{d})^{-2}\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup><caption>Exponent Property Review</caption>
      </table>
    
    
  
  <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  
  
  
  <table class="os-raise-textheavytable">
    <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
        <entry><emphasis>Expression</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Simplified Result</emphasis></entry></row>
        <row>
          <entry>
         \(j^5 \cdot j^3\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(j^8\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(\frac{h^7}{h^3}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
         \(h^4\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
         \((-ab)^0\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
        \(1\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \(\frac{1}{s^{-4}}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
         \(s^4\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
         \((\frac{m}{n})^{-4}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
         \(\frac{n^4}{m^4}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
        \((p^5)^2\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
        \(p^{10}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
         \((3s^3t^2)^3\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
         \(3^3s^9t^6 = 27s^9t^6\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((\frac{b}{d})^{-2}\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(\frac{d^2}{b^2}\)
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody></tgroup><caption>Exponent Property Review</caption>
    </table>
  
  

</solution></exercise>
</example><para>Take some time to review each of the exponential properties you learned in the lesson. Look at each property and be
  sure you know when to use it.</para>

<note>
  <para>Summary of Exponent Properties</para>
  
  <para>If \(a\) and \(b\) are real numbers and \(m\) and \(n\) are integers, then</para>
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
        <entry><emphasis>Property</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Description</emphasis></entry></row>
    <row>
        <entry> Product Property </entry>
        <entry> \(a^m \cdot a^n={a^{m+n}}\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Power Property </entry>
        <entry> \((a^m)^n=a^{m·n}\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Product to a Power </entry>
        <entry> \((ab)^m=a^mb^m\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Quotient Property </entry>
        <entry> \(\frac{a^m}{a^n}=a^{m−n}\), \(a\neq0\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Zero Exponent Property </entry>
        <entry> \(a^0=1\), \(a\neq0\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Quotient to a Power Property </entry>
        <entry> \((\frac{a}{b})^m=\frac{a^m}{b^m}\), \(b\neq0\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Properties of Negative Exponents </entry>
        <entry> \(a^{−n}=\frac{1}{a^n}\) and \(\frac{1}{a^{−n}}=a^n\) </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry> Quotient to a Negative Exponent </entry>
        <entry> \((\frac{a}{b})^{−n}=(\frac{b}{a})^n\) </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody></tgroup></table>
</note>
</section>
</content>
